ard. Both halves are P0. |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | E002 (bundled) — CSV export and stable API are delivery modes of the same per-project GPU-hour report data the P0 computation produces; they share the report data structure and API surface, so a split would build the same surface twice and is not separately schedulable. | |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | E003 (bundled) — the current-month consumption-vs-Kueue-quota view is presented in the same Dashboard administrator view surface over the same report data as HLR-1's viewing; not separately schedulable. | |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | E004 | Docs-authoring epic; priority P1 derived from strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` (docs-authoring priority exception — no priority inheritance). |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n   Teams table, no Dependencies table (the RHAISTRAT-9990 dependency appears\n   only as a frontmatter link), no formal Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria,\n   and no Non-Functional Requirements. Affected Components is a bare list\n   without per-component change/owner detail. Team assignments below were\n   inferred from the architecture-context owning teams (RHOAI Dashboard for\n   Dashboard; Distributed Workloads for Distributed Workloads) and should be\n   verified by a human.\n2. **Unstated backend locus (scope assumption to verify)**: the strategy does\n   not say where report computation lives. The decomposition assigns it to the\n   Distributed Workloads component because the Dashboard architecture context\n   states the Dashboard \"owns no data plane\" and speaks only the Kubernetes\n   API — so the reporting/export backend cannot be Dashboard work, and\n   Distributed Workloads is the only other affected component. If the intended\n   locus is elsewhere, E002's component/team should be corrected.\n3. **External timing risk**: the metering data schema finalizes only when\n   RHAISTRAT-9990 (in flight) lands. All Tier-2 epics carry that risk. It is\n   mitigated, not removed, by E001: validating the schema early and feeding\n   gaps back to the metering strategy while it can still change.\n4. **Docs epic team inferred**: the Documentation component has no\n   architecture-context file and the strategy names no docs owner; the docs\n   epic is assigned to the Distributed Workloads team because report semantics\n   (what counts as a GPU-hour) and export integration are defined by the\n   report computation. Verify with the actual documentation owner.\n5. **No priority inversions detected**: HLR-2 and HLR-3 are P1 but are bundled\n   into P0 epics on shared surfaces (see traceability rows); the docs epic is\n   P1 by the docs-authoring priority exception, not an inversion.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nThe external dependency (RHAISTRAT-9990 metering data, in flight, uncertain\ntiming) was evaluated for tiered delivery (Step 5.5). No user-facing partial\nvalue is deliverable before the metering data exists — every report and view\n(HLR-1/2/3) is computed from it — but risk-reduction work is independently\ndeliverable now:\n\n- **Tier 1 (independent, starts immediately)**: E001 — schema validation\n  against the metering strategy's design as it stands, producing early gap\n  feedback to RHAISTRAT-9990 while that strategy can still absorb changes.\n- **Tier 2 (dependency-gated)**: E002, E003, E004 — gated on the confirmed\n  schema (E001) and, for docs, on the completed implementations.\n\n## Component Mapping Notes\n\n- `Dashboard` and `Distributed Workloads` are used verbatim from\n  `.context/rhai-components.txt`.\n- The docs epic uses `Documentation` (canonical name). The strategy lists only\n  Dashboard and Distributed Workloads as affected; the Documentation component\n  is introduced by the decomposition to host the HLR-4 docs-authoring work, as\n  required by the work-product-type boundary rule.\n- E002 spans the strategy's metering-data consumption and export concerns;\n  `Distributed Workloads` is the single most-relevant canonical component (see\n  Health Warning 2).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43145,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e859950eb3df5e4","agent_id":"adf501cb0c82ea074","session_id":"dff1f5e9-7bd2-4936-ad2b-3d3b3c64229e","uuid":"82b0e80a-52af-460a-90be-14e837380f58","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:22:01.789Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
