{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f9bafb08-27a8-4c26-ab13-cccc26fe65b9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-823be3f1f0c93d09","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-k36ozruf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E001.md","content":"# Validate metering data schema against chargeback reporting needs\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the strategy's open question: the per-project\nGPU-hour usage data schema owned by the in-flight GPU usage metering strategy\n(RHAISTRAT-9990) is not final until that strategy lands, and the chargeback\nreporting built in this strategy consumes it. The investigation confirms what\nthe landed schema provides, validates that it supports every chargeback\nreporting need, and produces a written consumption mapping plus a gap report\nthat can be fed back to the metering strategy while it can still change.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Review the metering data schema as designed/delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990\n  (per-project GPU-hour usage data), tracking it to finalization.\n- Produce a consumption mapping from the schema's elements to the chargeback\n  reporting needs: per-project attribution, selectable time-range aggregation,\n  current-month rollup, and export/API retrieval.\n- Evaluate each reporting requirement against the schema and mark it supported\n  or gap-identified, with a proposed schema remediation for each gap.\n- Deliver the gap report to the metering strategy owners so gaps can be\n  addressed before that strategy lands.\n- Recommend whether the reporting implementation can proceed on the current\n  schema or must wait for remediation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written consumption mapping exists that maps each relevant metering schema\n  element to the chargeback reporting needs (per-project attribution,\n  selectable time ranges, current-month rollup).\n- Every reporting requirement (per-project GPU-hour reports, time-range\n  selection, current-month consumption vs Kueue quota comparison, CSV export,\n  API retrieval) is evaluated against the schema and marked either supported\n  or gap-identified, and each identified gap carries a proposed remediation.\n- A gap report is delivered to the metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990) owners.\n- A go/no-go recommendation documents whether the reporting implementation can\n  proceed on the current schema or must wait for remediation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): the schema validation confirms the data foundation for\n  per-project GPU-hour consumption reports; gates the report computation and\n  the administrator views.\n- HLR-2 (P1): export/API retrieval requirements are among the needs validated\n  against the schema.\n- HLR-3 (P1): current-month rollup and quota-comparison data needs are among\n  the needs validated against the schema.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The metering schema finalizes only when RHAISTRAT-9990 lands; this\n  investigation's completion is therefore exposed to that strategy's timing.\n  Early validation of the draft design is the mitigation — gaps found now can\n  still be fixed upstream.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45123,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e859950eb3df5e4","agent_id":"adf501cb0c82ea074","session_id":"dff1f5e9-7bd2-4936-ad2b-3d3b3c64229e","uuid":"1b34b68f-2dee-4ff7-bf45-f978ba71cbd5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:22:11.784Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
