{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f9bafb08-27a8-4c26-ab13-cccc26fe65b9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd87fbd9a2c17614","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-k36ozruf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E002.md","content":"# Per-project GPU-hour report computation, CSV export and stable API\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the reporting backend for GPU chargeback: computation of\nper-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges from the\nmetering data delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990),\nCSV export of those reports, and a stable API through which finance tooling\ncan retrieve them. It consumes the metering data as delivered and does not\nre-implement usage collection (explicitly out of scope for this strategy).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Compute per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over\n  administrator-selectable time ranges from the metering data.\n- Provide CSV export of the reports.\n- Provide a stable API for retrieving reports, suitable for finance tooling\n  integration.\n- Consume the metering data exactly as delivered by the metering strategy —\n  no duplication of the collection pipeline.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given metered per-project GPU-hour usage data, the computed report for a\n  selected time range matches the aggregated GPU-hours per project for that\n  range.\n- Reports are exportable as CSV.\n- Reports are retrievable via a stable API usable by finance tooling.\n- The computation consumes the metering data as delivered by the metering\n  strategy and contains no usage-collection logic (out-of-scope guard).\n- The report computation is validated against the confirmed metering data\n  schema before integration (gated by the schema validation outcome; if the\n  landed schema differs from the reporting assumptions, the consumption\n  mapping is re-derived before this epic's approach is finalized).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time\n  ranges, computed from the metering data — the computation half of this HLR\n  (the administrator-facing viewing half is delivered by the Dashboard work).\n- HLR-2 (P1, bundled): CSV export and stable API retrieval — delivery modes\n  of the same report data the P0 computation produces; they share the report\n  data structure and API surface, so they are not separately schedulable and\n  stay bundled with the HLR-1 computation.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- External timing risk: the metering data schema finalizes only when\n  RHAISTRAT-9990 lands; this epic starts only after the schema validation\n  confirms the data foundation.\n- Reports are in GPU-hours, not dollars — currency/cost-rate modelling is out\n  of scope.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45123,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e859950eb3df5e4","agent_id":"adf501cb0c82ea074","session_id":"dff1f5e9-7bd2-4936-ad2b-3d3b3c64229e","uuid":"7323de20-c2d8-429f-ab9a-5eb06e6400c5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:22:18.533Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
