{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f9bafb08-27a8-4c26-ab13-cccc26fe65b9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8306e7d8928bfeeb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-k36ozruf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E003.md","content":"# Dashboard administrator chargeback reporting views\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the administrator-facing chargeback reporting experience in\nthe Dashboard: platform administrators can view per-project GPU-hour\nconsumption reports over selectable time ranges, and see current-month\nconsumption against each project's Kueue quota. The Dashboard presents report\ndata computed by the reporting backend — it does not recompute consumption\n(the Dashboard owns no data plane) — and reads Kueue quota from the platform's\nexisting queueing CRs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Administrator view of per-project GPU-hour consumption reports with\n  selectable time ranges, surfacing the report data provided by the reporting\n  backend delivered under this strategy.\n- Administrator view showing current-month consumption against each project's\n  Kueue quota.\n- Restrict the chargeback reporting views to platform administrators.\n- Consume report data from the reporting capability — no re-aggregation or\n  recomputation of GPU-hours in the Dashboard.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- An administrator can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports for a\n  selectable time range, with figures matching the reporting backend's output\n  for that range.\n- An administrator can see current-month consumption shown against each\n  project's Kueue quota.\n- Consumption figures displayed in the Dashboard are surfaced from the\n  reporting backend without recomputation in the Dashboard.\n- The chargeback reporting views are visible only to platform administrators.\n- The views are validated against the confirmed metering data schema\n  dimensions (gated by the schema validation outcome; if the available data\n  dimensions differ, the view scope is re-derived).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption\n  reports over selectable time ranges — the viewing half of this HLR (the\n  computation half is delivered by the reporting backend work).\n- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the current-month consumption-vs-Kueue-quota view is\n  presented in the same administrator view surface over the same report data\n  as the HLR-1 viewing; it is not separately schedulable and stays bundled.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Depends on the reporting backend's report data surface being available;\n  the Dashboard builds against it (the Dashboard owns no data plane and\n  speaks the Kubernetes API per its architecture context).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45123,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e859950eb3df5e4","agent_id":"adf501cb0c82ea074","session_id":"dff1f5e9-7bd2-4936-ad2b-3d3b3c64229e","uuid":"b52cd794-fd28-41b0-b8d9-4d290bd3f334","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:22:24.819Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
