{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9937f4f892674747","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n3\ttitle: Per-project GPU-hour report computation, CSV export and stable API\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the landed metering schema cannot support per-project GPU-hour\n15\t    attribution or the required time-range aggregation, feed the gaps back to the\n16\t    metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990), re-derive the consumption mapping, and rewrite\n17\t    the report computation against the remediated schema; scope reporting to the dimensions\n18\t    the landed schema supports if remediation is delayed.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 0\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 0\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Per-project GPU-hour report computation, CSV export and stable API\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic delivers the reporting backend for GPU chargeback: computation of\n41\tper-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges from the\n42\tmetering data delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990),\n43\tCSV export of those reports, and a stable API through which finance tooling\n44\tcan retrieve them. It consumes the metering data as delivered and does not\n45\tre-implement usage collection (explicitly out of scope for this strategy).\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Compute per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over\n50\t  administrator-selectable time ranges from the metering data.\n51\t- Provide CSV export of the reports.\n52\t- Provide a stable API for retrieving reports, suitable for finance tooling\n53\t  integration.\n54\t- Consume the metering data exactly as delivered by the metering strategy —\n55\t  no duplication of the collection pipeline.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given metered per-project GPU-hour usage data, the computed report for a\n60\t  selected time range matches the aggregated GPU-hours per project for that\n61\t  range.\n62\t- Reports are exportable as CSV.\n63\t- Reports are retrievable via a stable API usable by finance tooling.\n64\t- The computation consumes the metering data as delivered by the metering\n65\t  strategy and contains no usage-collection logic (out-of-scope guard).\n66\t- The report computation is validated against the confirmed metering data\n67\t  schema before integration (gated by the schema validation outcome; if the\n68\t  landed schema differs from the reporting assumptions, the consumption\n69\t  mapping is re-derived before this epic's approach is finalized).\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-1 (P0): per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time\n74\t  ranges, computed from the metering data — the computation half of this HLR\n75\t  (the administrator-facing viewing half is delivered by the Dashboard work).\n76\t- HLR-2 (P1, bundled): CSV export and stable API retrieval — delivery modes\n77\t  of the same report data the P0 computation produces; they share the report\n78\t  data structure and API surface, so they are not separately schedulable and\n79\t  stay bundled with the HLR-1 computation.\n80\t\n81\t## Risks / Notes\n82\t\n83\t- External timing risk: the metering data schema finalizes only when\n84\t  RHAISTRAT-9990 lands; this epic starts only after the schema validation\n85\t  confirms the data foundation.\n86\t- Reports are in GPU-hours, not dollars — currency/cost-rate modelling is out\n87\t  of scope.\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89248bb50d0e427b","agent_id":"aaafc8d5c544774e9","session_id":"dff1f5e9-7bd2-4936-ad2b-3d3b3c64229e","uuid":"1e6bdb0b-728f-451d-8847-ef79e7fb896d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:24:23.791Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9937f4f892674747","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
