e report data provided by the reporting\n52\t  backend delivered under this strategy.\n53\t- Administrator view showing current-month consumption against each project's\n54\t  Kueue quota.\n55\t- Restrict the chargeback reporting views to platform administrators.\n56\t- Consume report data from the reporting capability — no re-aggregation or\n57\t  recomputation of GPU-hours in the Dashboard.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- An administrator can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports for a\n62\t  selectable time range, with figures matching the reporting backend's output\n63\t  for that range.\n64\t- An administrator can see current-month consumption shown against each\n65\t  project's Kueue quota.\n66\t- Consumption figures displayed in the Dashboard are surfaced from the\n67\t  reporting backend without recomputation in the Dashboard.\n68\t- The chargeback reporting views are visible only to platform administrators.\n69\t- The views are validated against the confirmed metering data schema\n70\t  dimensions (gated by the schema validation outcome; if the available data\n71\t  dimensions differ, the view scope is re-derived).\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-1 (P0): administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption\n76\t  reports over selectable time ranges — the viewing half of this HLR (the\n77\t  computation half is delivered by the reporting backend work).\n78\t- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the current-month consumption-vs-Kueue-quota view is\n79\t  presented in the same administrator view surface over the same report data\n80\t  as the HLR-1 viewing; it is not separately schedulable and stays bundled.\n81\t\n82\t## Risks / Notes\n83\t\n84\t- Depends on the reporting backend's report data surface being available;\n85\t  the Dashboard builds against it (the Dashboard owns no data plane and\n86\t  speaks the Kubernetes API per its architecture context).\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89248bb50d0e427b","agent_id":"